  "summary": "A majority of Burlingame City Council supports exploring a citywide surveillance technology policy to govern data access, auditing, and purpose limitations for tools like its 17 Flock ALPR cameras. Mayor Brownrigg cited national distrust of law enforcement and incidents in nearby cities like Mountain View as motivation, while two councilmembers expressed reservations about added bureaucracy.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "In nearby Mountain View, for example, federal and state law enforcement agencies accessed the ALPR data in violation of city policy, spurring community concern and an end to the program.",
      "paragraph_idx": 3
    },
    {
      "quote": "I am confident our department is treating this data sensitively. Unfortunately, the world isn't Burlingame.",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "I would be interested in pursuing a policy. I understand we would be the first in the county putting something together, but I don't think that should prohibit us from doing so.",
      "paragraph_idx": 8
    }
  ],
